{
  "_doc": "Destruction rules (Phase 4; PLAN §8, research/destruction.md). Every destructible surface is a panel: a grid of square cells about `cellM` wide (an engine setting, PLAN §8.2, not a Siege value), in layers through its thickness: a front and a back skin and a core (wooden studs in walls, metal joists in floors, beams in hatches), plus a steel layer once reinforced. `constructions` describe a panel's build; `surfaces` give the construction a level solid of that surface gets unless it names another (HARD_WALL, HARD_FLOOR, PROP and INGREDIENT stay solid until later phases). Bullets: a weapon's destruction tier (Siege's label in Detailed Weapon Stats) comes from its weapon file, or `classTiers` where the file has none; the tier's rules (adjusted per class by `classAdjust`) make holes of `holeDiameterM` in every layer a pellet passes, remove studs only if `studs` (buckshot only within `studsWithinM`), and cost a whole breakable panel (hatch, barricade, glass) `hatchDamage` or `barricadeDamage` points per pellet. Through each panel a bullet's damage is multiplied by `wallbang.damageMult`, and it passes at most `wallbang.maxSurfaces` panels. `explosives` are the shapes the Destruction Lab's tools cut (their gadgets, throws and damage come in Phase 8): `hard` cuts steel, `studs` cuts wooden studs. Distances in metres, times in seconds.",
